WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.421
Meet Aperture, a competitive intelligence
workspace for biopharma teams.

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:09.706
Let’s follow one question from the first
research brief to a strategy meeting.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:14.371
Suppose your team works on
elranatamab in multiple myeloma.

00:00:14.551 --> 00:00:19.606
Which other bispecific antibodies should you
track in the fourth-line setting and beyond?

00:00:20.547 --> 00:00:21.873
Start in Ask mode.

00:00:21.873 --> 00:00:26.922
The AI consultant proposes competitors,
trials, and sources to check.

00:00:27.102 --> 00:00:29.597
You narrow the shortlist to three rivals,

00:00:29.597 --> 00:00:31.830
then switch to Edit to build the landscape.

00:00:32.755 --> 00:00:35.779
The studies come in
from ClinicalTrials.gov.

00:00:35.779 --> 00:00:39.367
Each registry record keeps its
identifier and source link.

00:00:39.547 --> 00:00:42.985
Open a study to check its
design, enrollment, and dates.

00:00:43.922 --> 00:00:46.204
Now the team can see the field.

00:00:46.204 --> 00:00:49.838
The landscape places each
program at its development stage.

00:00:50.018 --> 00:00:52.830
Group by target, and a difference emerges.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:56.000
Three drugs share a target.
One takes another route.

00:00:56.922 --> 00:01:00.534
Switch to the timeline to
see which trials overlap

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:02.567
and when their primary
endpoints are expected.

00:01:02.747 --> 00:01:07.560
The catalyst calendar collects the milestones
worth bringing to the next team review.

00:01:08.505 --> 00:01:11.448
In Benchmarks, open a response result

00:01:11.448 --> 00:01:14.789
to see which patients it describes
and where it was reported.

00:01:14.969 --> 00:01:18.859
That context matters when the trials
enrolled different populations.

00:01:19.797 --> 00:01:21.867
Which rival deserves a closer look?

00:01:21.867 --> 00:01:23.915
On the overview, change the lens.

00:01:24.095 --> 00:01:27.437
Market entry, enrollment,
and molecular similarity

00:01:27.437 --> 00:01:29.470
each give you a ranking with reasons.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.263
Now ask the copilot why
one rival sits apart.

00:01:33.443 --> 00:01:38.591
It identifies talquetamab
as the one targeting GPRC5D.

00:01:38.591 --> 00:01:41.718
The other three target BCMA.

00:01:41.898 --> 00:01:44.310
That gives the team a sharper follow-up.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:47.850
What evidence do we have
after prior BCMA therapy?

00:01:48.797 --> 00:01:51.981
Save the answer as a
brief, review its wording,

00:01:51.981 --> 00:01:53.301
and share it with the dashboard.

00:01:53.481 --> 00:01:57.763
For the strategy meeting, export the
landscape as an editable PowerPoint.

00:01:58.713 --> 00:02:01.835
Aperture. Clinical strategy, in focus.
